@doc """
What one parser call found in a buffer.

`Complete` carries the message and the bytes that came after it. On
a keep-alive connection those bytes are the start of the next
message.

`Incomplete` means the buffer does not hold a whole message yet.
Read more bytes, append them, and call the parser again.
"""
enum Parser.Outcome<T>
  Complete((T, Binary))
  Incomplete
end
